'''Mozbayana''' ({{Langx|mxi|مستبانية|Mozbâniya}}; {{Langx|bl|Mozarabya|4=land of the [[Mozbayán]]}}) is a loosely defined [[W:Cultural region|cultural]] and historic region located in the territory of [[Balisca]]. In the 21st century, the concept has re-emerged out of a desire for {{W|sovereignty}}, {{W|self-determination}}, and {{W|self-governance}} in areas where Mozbayán culture, the [[Mozarabic|Mozarabic language]], and Mozbayán identity have been based. Alternative names historically used for the region include ''Arrayán'' (الرَيْحَان‎; ''ar-rayḥān'', "myrtle"), in a similar naming pattern of [[Araucaria]].

'''Mozbayán nationalism''' ({{lang-bl|nacionalismo mozbayana}}) is an ideology (primarily {{W|regionalism|regionalist}}) and political movement active mostly in the [[Cabu Verd]], as well as in other parts of Balisca in which the [[W:Privateers|privateers]] and pirates of the [[Hesperian League]] and [[Maroon Confederacy]] were active, such as [[Cabu Traïdor]] and isolated areas of [[Pindorama]]. Most Mozarabic nationalists consider Mozarabia to distinct nationality within Balisca. The ideology is mainly promoted by the [[W:Platformism|platform]] ''[[Mozarabya Existe]]'' (ME).

Generally speaking, Mozbayán nationalists promote their distinct identity and the rediscovery of the [[Maroon Confederacy]]'s heritage, traditions, culture, and language and/or demand increased autonomy of the Mozbayán-speaking territories. 

